; ============================================================
;  THE POUCH LADDER - ELEVEN POUCHES IN THREE COLOURS
;
;  They fit a chest rig's two pouch slots and grant REAL POCKETS: a
;  magazine in a yellow one is in your loadout and feeds a reload.
;
;    GREEN  g1-g4   single squares. Food, drink, devices and bandages
;                   are quick from them. Cheap capacity.
;    YELLOW y1-y5   magazine pockets. Nothing is quick; reloads draw
;                   from here.
;    RED    r1-r2   green plus the whole pharmacy, medkits included.
;                   The only pockets a medkit is fast from, and the
;                   line STOPS AT TWO on purpose - it sells one thing
;                   and you only need a little of it.
;
;  RED IS THE ONLY SOURCE OF A RED SQUARE. Rigs have none at all now,
;  at any tier - so a medic's pouch is not a luxury on top of what the
;  rig gave you, it IS what you have. Two pouch slots, so the ceiling
;  is four fast medical squares and the floor is nought.
;
;  A FLOOR OF NOUGHT IS LIVABLE because a GREEN square is quick for
;  BANDAGES, and every rig has three to six. Only medkits and the rest
;  of the pharmacy need red.
;
;  SO RED CAME DOWN, from 12,000 a square to 4,000. It was priced as a
;  prize when it was the thing you bought ON TOP of a rig's own two or
;  three. As the only source, that price was a wall rather than a
;  choice. Still three times green, and still the dearest square in
;  the game per cell.
;
;  AND GREEN CAME DOWN TOO, to 1,200 a square, because rig recipes buy
;  green squares by the handful now and a rig should not cost more to
;  make than to buy.
;
;  ONE CELL EACH, AND A SHEET OF OUR OWN.
;
;  inv_grid_width is not only a footprint - it is also how much of the
;  atlas is sampled - so a pouch cannot be one cell in the bag while
;  wearing a picture drawn across two. These eleven have their own
;  50x50 icons in ui\ui_sa_tiers_pouches, cut down from the Layered
;  addon's art, washed with the colour of the pockets they grant, and
;  numbered.
;
;  So a pouch takes ONE square in your bag instead of four, a colour
;  is legible at a glance, and the tier is readable without hovering -
;  which three separate attempts with inherited pictures could not do,
;  because three parents cannot give eleven faces.
;
;  The parent still matters: mag_limit_small/medium/large come from
;  it, and that is what a rig reads before it will accept a pouch at
;  all. Only the picture is overridden.
;
;  THE OLD ARRANGEMENT, for reference:
;
;      yellow -> af_magpouch_s     the small pouch picture
;      green  -> af_magpouch_m     the medium
;      red    -> af_magpouch_l     for the fields, but it is DRAWN
;                                   with the Layered addon's medical
;                                   pouch - the one with the red cross
;                                   on it, which says what the pouch
;                                   is better than any magazine pouch
;                                   picture could
;
;  The pairing is arbitrary and that is fine - what matters is that
;  one colour is one picture. This one puts the magazine pouches on
;  the picture that has magazines in it, which is the only one of the
;  three that says anything about its contents.
;
;  So a colour is one look, every time, and eleven pouches read as
;  three families rather than as eleven strangers. All three stock
;  pictures are the same 2x2 footprint, so nothing changes size.
;
;  THE PARENT IS ALSO THE ELIGIBILITY. mag_limit_small/medium/large
;  come with it, and those are what A.is_pouch_sec reads when a rig
;  decides whether to accept the thing at all - a duplicate that did
;  not inherit one of these three would be refused by the rig without
;  a word.
;
;  IT IS A PLACEHOLDER AND IT LOOKS LIKE ONE. The small pouch picture
;  has magazines standing in it, which is an odd face on a pouch that
;  holds bread. Distinct art per pouch is an icon sheet - see the
;  README.
;
;  WHAT EACH GRANTS is one line per section in
;  items/settings/zzz_amp_pouch_grants.ltx - including its COLOUR,
;  which is the only thing separating a green square from a red one.
; ============================================================

